  "notes": "Fighting passage: only what the tafsirs say with their restrictions (the treaty-holders of that time, the four months, those who broke oaths and attacked); no battle, weapon, captive or killing drawn; no present-day reading. No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. 5:1-4 carries As-Sa'di's restriction (the four months, and the full term for longer treaties). The command itself (5:5-14) is left unglossed: no chip may read as a general call. An hourglass for the months ending, light for repentance, a house for «فأجره», a book for «كلام الله», footsteps for «أبلغه مأمنه». STAGING v4: Fighting and treaty passage: stays ambient (owner rule, Staging v4). In 6 the words addressed to the Prophet (6:5-6 and 6:12) get no plate: the house plate moves to 6:13 (his place of safety, As-Sa'di: the place where he is safe) and the footsteps plate is dropped; the light plate over 6:8-10 becomes a geometric plate on 6:9-10 (the speech of Allah is His attribute: no light plate there)."
